<title>CANADA: Polygram's Canada film proposal opposed.</title>
<headline>Polygram's Canada film proposal opposed.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The official opposition in Canada's Parliament urged the Liberal government on Wednesday to block PolyGram NV from distributing independent movies in Canada.</p>
<p>&quot;(Industry) Minister John Manley must turn down this request,&quot; said Gaston Leroux, spokesman on cultural matters for the separatist Bloc Quebecois, in a statement.</p>
<p>The Dutch company's PolyGram Filmed Entertainment unit is seeking exemption from strict rules intended to protect Canadian film distributors and producers, promising in return to invest heavily in the Canadian film industry.</p>
</text>
